From e136d42588bf460460133485b8f7b63fe874edfa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kara <kara@soulstone.org>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 17:59:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fetcher: send Status::Done when the index completes

Status::Done is sent on the want_length == 0 path (everything already
on disk at startup), but a fetch that actually downloads its pieces
returns State::Done from the ValidPiece handler without ever sending
Status::Done. Anything consuming subscribe_status() as the completion
signal waits forever on a fetch that has finished.

Found embedding stigmerge-peer in another application whose
orchestration waited on the status channel; the fetched file was
byte-perfect while the process sat waiting.
---
 stigmerge-peer/src/fetcher.rs | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/stigmerge-peer/src/fetcher.rs b/stigmerge-peer/src/fetcher.rs
index de31afa..982325f 100644
--- a/stigmerge-peer/src/fetcher.rs
+++ b/stigmerge-peer/src/fetcher.rs
@@ -417,6 +417,13 @@ impl<C: Connection + Clone + Send + Sync + 'static> Fetcher<C> {
                                 }
                             });
                             if index_complete {
+                                // Status::Done is already sent on the
+                                // nothing-to-fetch path above; a fetch that
+                                // actually downloaded pieces returned
+                                // State::Done without ever saying so on the
+                                // status channel, so consumers of
+                                // subscribe_status waited forever.
+                                self.status_tx.send_replace(Status::Done);
                                 task_cancel.cancel();
                                 return Ok(State::Done);
                             }
